<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Shakespeare returns four weeks after the propranolol dose was increased to 80 mg each morning. He has had two occupational therapy sessions: he now writes with a weighted, wide-grip pen, rests his forearm on the desk, writes a little larger and slower, and dictates long drafts. He can sign his name steadily if he signs halfway down a page rather than at the very foot. He has had no dizziness, wheeze, cold hands, fatigue, or low mood. He has kept within the agreed limits since the brief intervention ten weeks ago, at about 10 drinks a week with no day above three for the last five, and two cups of coffee. He feels his hand is his own again. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 80 mg for four weeks; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational therapy</td><td>Two sessions; weighted wide-grip pen, forearm support, dictation</td></tr><tr><td>Writing</td><td>Full pages legible; signature steady</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Within limits for ten weeks; about 10 drinks a week for the last five</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

