    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential tremor (G25.0)</content>. Good response to propranolol 80 mg with occupational therapy: TETRAS performance 12 (from 22 at diagnosis), activities of daily living 9 (from 18), writing item 1.5. Pulse 62 and blood pressure 120/76 mmHg without side effects. [S]<list><item>Continue propranolol extended-release 80 mg each morning.</item><item>Continue the occupational therapy techniques.</item><item>Review in three months; sooner if the tremor changes or new signs appear.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hazardous drinking (Z72.89)</content>. Ten weeks within the agreed limits; GGT 49 U/L (from 84), ALT 30 and AST 29 U/L: the liver tests have normalized. [S]<list><item>Keep to the limits; repeat AUDIT at the next preventive visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Tremor rating: TETRAS performance and activities of daily living subscales</td><td>At each visit while treatment is adjusted</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Performance 12 (from 22) and activities of daily living 9 (from 18); writing item 1.5</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Archimedes spiral and handwriting sample (the same sentence each time, dated and kept in the chart)</td><td>At each visit while treatment is adjusted</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Right spiral close to the left, with a small tremor axis; handwriting even and legible across a full page</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Beta-blocker safety: resting pulse, seated and standing blood pressure, wheeze, fatigue, cold hands, low mood, exercise tolerance</td><td>At each visit after starting or changing the dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Pulse 62; blood pressure 120/76 mmHg with no postural drop; no wheeze, fatigue, cold hands, or low mood</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Drinking review after the brief intervention (drinks a week, heaviest day, use of alcohol to steady the hand)</td><td>At each visit after a brief intervention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 10 drinks a week for the last five weeks, no day above three; within limits for ten weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>GGT and liver tests after reducing alcohol</td><td>Eight to twelve weeks after the brief intervention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GGT 49 U/L (from 84), ALT 30 U/L, AST 29 U/L</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational therapy for writing</td><td>When tremor limits writing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two sessions completed; techniques in use</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>Once, then when health or wishes change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Discussed at the preventive visit; health care agent named</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Primidone (sedation, unsteadiness, nausea)</td><td>Only if used</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not started; propranolol is effective and tolerated</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Brain MRI or dopamine transporter imaging</td><td>Only for atypical features (rest tremor, parkinsonism, asymmetry with other signs, sudden onset, ataxia)</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No atypical features; the diagnosis is clinical</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Deep brain stimulation or focused ultrasound thalamotomy</td><td>Only for disabling tremor despite adequate trials of two first-line drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Tremor responding to the first drug</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Classify the tremor and exclude treatable causes by the second visit. Outcome by 2026-01-26: Essential tremor diagnosed; TSH, glucose, calcium, and kidney tests normal; no parkinsonism [S]</item><item>Legible handwriting for a full page and a steady signature. In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>No more than 14 standard drinks a week and no more than 4 on any day. In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>Resting pulse above 55 without dizziness, wheeze, or fatigue on propranolol. In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011; reaffirmed 2025) (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019); Unhealthy Alcohol Use in Adolescents and Adults: Screening and Behavioral Counseling Interventions (2018); Helping Patients Who Drink Too Much: A Clinician&apos;s Guide (2005); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Tremor review in three months; second zoster dose due in the next two months; he has not yet returned the fecal immunochemical test kit and was reminded today. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
